# Git for Windows checks files out with CRLF by default (core.autocrlf=true in
# its own system gitconfig). These files are read by Linux inside the containers,
# where CRLF is not cosmetic: a shebang becomes "#!/bin/bash\r", the kernel looks
# for an interpreter literally named /bin/bash\r, and the container dies with
# "exec ./entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory".
#
# So they stay LF in the working tree, whatever the platform or the developer's
# core.autocrlf.

*.sh    text eol=lf
*.cnf   text eol=lf
